<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">2004 Summer Olympics</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2004">2004</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Also known as Athens 2004</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 2004 Summer Olympics were held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> from 13 to 29 August 2004, bringing the Games back to the city of the first modern Olympics of 1896. More than 10,000 athletes from 201 national Olympic committees took part. Preparations gave Athens a new airport, metro lines and a tram, but the cost of the venues added to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>'s public debt.</p></div>
